{"href":"/en/tip/33-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"For long‑term wheelchair users, switch to a pressure‑relieving cushion and check the ischial and sacrococcygeal areas daily"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Don’t buy therapies or devices that claim to cure paralysis, blindness, or deafness"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After obtaining the disability certificate, visit the county-level civil affairs bureau to ask about all available benefits at once"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"For children under 7 who have disabilities or autism, apply to the county-level civil affairs bureau for rehabilitation assistance"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Families can apply to local civil affairs bureaus at or above the county level for subsidies to modify ramps, handrails, and bathrooms at home"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Mentioning your disability certificate during a job interview can save the employer money"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Tax reductions for individuals with disabilities – how much can be saved? Call your provincial tax bureau for details"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Guide dogs are allowed in public places and on public transport; blind individuals ride city buses for free"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Disabled candidates taking the national college entrance exam can request reasonable accommodations, including a 50% time extension for those using Braille test papers"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Schools may not refuse enrollment for children with disabilities; those unable to attend receive in‑home instruction arranged by the education bureau"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"People missing their right lower limb or both lower limbs can still obtain a driver’s license; the designated category is C5"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Rehabilitation should be carried out at a proper facility with a rehabilitation medicine department; the intensity must be set by therapists — more intensity does not necessarily mean better results"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/33-17","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Getting a hearing aid when hearing declines — the reason is to hear better now, not to prevent dementia"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Saying an adult “can’t manage his own affairs” requires a court determination; family members can’t decide on their own"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Guardians for adults are appointed in a legal order; if the ward injures someone, the guardian must pay compensation"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"If you’re denied a job, denied promotion, or paid less because of a disability, you can sue — but first calculate the associated costs"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/33"},"children":["Chapter 33"," ·"," ","How to live after becoming disabled"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"33-17"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["17"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Getting a hearing aid when hearing declines — the reason is to hear better now, not to prevent dementia"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["The claim that “wearing a hearing aid prevents dementia” currently lacks solid evidence. A three‑year trial involving nearly a thousand participants found no overall difference between groups. Only among people already at higher risk of cognitive decline did a modest benefit appear. Thus, the main reason to get a hearing aid is to hear clearly now — to talk with others and hear traffic while crossing the street — not to protect the brain decades later."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Hearing aids cost several thousand to tens of thousands of…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["The ACHIEVE trial took place in four U.S. communities and enrolled 977 individuals aged 70–84 with untreated h…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Getting a hearing aid when hearing declines — the reason is to hear better now, not to prevent dementia"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children"